WEBVTT

NOTE
Journey: Advocates - Week 25 Student Video
Unit 7, Lesson 1: Evil

1
00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:10.690
My father has taught me many valuable life lessons.

2
00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:15.610
One lesson in particular, which came from his father, my grandfather, is that a

3
00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.670
problem well defined is half solved.

4
00:00:19.050 --> 00:00:23.870
In other words, if we can clearly define the nature of a problem, we're halfway

5
00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:25.930
towards finding a viable solution.

6
00:00:26.910 --> 00:00:32.270
Undoubtedly, the problem of evil is one of the greatest challenges raised against

7
00:00:32.270 --> 00:00:35.930
the Christian faith, or really against any belief system.

8
00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:41.330
But before we ask the question why might God allow evil or how does a Christian

9
00:00:41.330 --> 00:00:47.110
faith make sense of evil, let's first make sure we clearly define evil.

10
00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:52.670
Not too long ago I was in getting my hair cut and I overheard a conversation next to

11
00:00:52.670 --> 00:00:57.170
me that quickly caught my attention because the conversation was about the problem

12
00:00:57.170 --> 00:01:02.710
of suffering and evil. And a lady said this she said I think evil and good are

13
00:01:02.710 --> 00:01:08.510
equal but opposing forces I had to jump in as soon as I heard this

14
00:01:08.510 --> 00:01:13.350
because it seems to me that she gave a faulty view of the nature of evil you see

15
00:01:13.350 --> 00:01:19.290
good and evil are not two equal opposing forces rather evil is a corruption

16
00:01:19.290 --> 00:01:25.230
of good you see you can have good without evil but you cannot have evil

17
00:01:25.230 --> 00:01:30.910
unless you first have a standard of good that can be corrupted consider an example

18
00:01:30.910 --> 00:01:36.450
from C.S. Lewis, a former atheist, by the way, that he wrote in his classic book,

19
00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:42.550
Mere Christianity. My argument against God was that the universe seemed so cruel and

20
00:01:42.550 --> 00:01:46.930
unjust. But how had I got this idea of just and unjust?

21
00:01:47.290 --> 00:01:51.770
A man does not call a line crooked unless he has some idea of a straight line.

22
00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:55.630
What was I comparing this universe with when I called it unjust?

23
00:01:56.570 --> 00:02:02.350
As Lewis noted, justice and injustice are not equal and opposite forces.

24
00:02:03.110 --> 00:02:07.170
Injustice is parasitic upon a standard of justice.

25
00:02:07.570 --> 00:02:12.770
You cannot call a line crooked unless you first have a standard of a straight line.

26
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:16.890
Consider another example, let's take truth and lies.

27
00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:20.890
Truth is when a belief matches up with reality.

28
00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:24.630
In a sense truth is telling it like it is.

29
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:30.070
A lie is when you tell something that intentionally doesn't match up with reality.

30
00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:34.270
It's intentionally saying something that doesn't tell it like it is.

31
00:02:34.410 --> 00:02:39.290
You see, you can have truth of which no one tells a lie but you cannot tell lie

32
00:02:39.290 --> 00:02:44.790
unless there's first truth. Lies are a corruption of truth.

33
00:02:45.530 --> 00:02:50.830
This idea that evil is a corruption of good is evident in the broken

34
00:02:50.830 --> 00:02:55.910
world around us. Divorce is a broken marriage.

35
00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:02.510
Racism results from broken relationships where we fail to recognize diversity.

36
00:03:03.450 --> 00:03:08.690
And addiction results from taking something meant for good, food, technology,

37
00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:13.470
medicine, sex, and corrupting it for something bad.

38
00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:18.930
Simply put, evil is when things are not the way they're supposed to be or they

39
00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.050
are the way they're not supposed to be.

40
00:03:21.430 --> 00:03:27.130
Understood this way, evil assumes that there is a way the world in fact is

41
00:03:27.130 --> 00:03:33.070
supposed to be. But this only makes sense if there's really purpose and intent and a

42
00:03:33.070 --> 00:03:36.210
mind and design behind the world.

43
00:03:36.670 --> 00:03:42.430
So raising the problem of evil actually assumes and implies that there is

44
00:03:42.430 --> 00:03:45.550
a way that the world is supposed to function.

45
00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:52.330
but atheism cannot account for design or purpose or the claim that the world is

46
00:03:52.330 --> 00:03:57.850
supposed to be a certain way and the reason is because on atheism the world just is

47
00:03:57.850 --> 00:04:02.570
it popped into existence from nothing and through time and chance and the laws of

48
00:04:02.570 --> 00:04:08.290
physics the world just arranged itself in the way we see it today so ironically

49
00:04:08.290 --> 00:04:13.550
if an atheist complains about the problem of evil they have to assume the theistic

50
00:04:13.550 --> 00:04:15.210
worldview to do so.

51
00:04:16.130 --> 00:04:20.090
Pantheists also can't consistently raise the problem of evil.

52
00:04:20.290 --> 00:04:24.810
And the reason is because on pantheism, as you'll remember, distinctions are

53
00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:30.410
artificial. There really is no distinction between me and you, mind and matter,

54
00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:33.990
yesterday and yesterday, good and evil.

55
00:04:34.670 --> 00:04:40.230
So according to pantheism, you can't have a problem of evil because evil doesn't

56
00:04:40.230 --> 00:04:46.110
exist it's an illusion properly understood the existence of evil is one

57
00:04:46.110 --> 00:04:50.750
good reason to believe there's a standard of good and if there's a standard of good

58
00:04:50.750 --> 00:04:56.730
the best explanation is that there's a God now this doesn't explain why God allows evil

59
00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:02.330
we'll get to that but at this point it's critical to realize when we properly define

60
00:05:02.330 --> 00:05:05.070
and understand the nature of evil.

61
00:05:05.190 --> 00:05:09.830
It's one good reason to believe that God actually exists.

